Ibrahim Saleh: Heads up from today's UX pass: our global keyboard shortcuts bar (press "?") opens an overlay but VoiceOver reads the content twice and sometimes doesn't move focus into the overlay. Repro on macOS Safari and Chrome.
Keiko Tanaka: Repro on my machine. It looks like we're toggling aria-hidden on the app while also setting focus programmatically which confuses SRs. Also the overlay content uses role=document instead of dialog.
Sasha Lee: Two problems: 1) overlay should be role=dialog with aria-modal=true; 2) when opening, move focus to the dialog heading (tabindex='-1'). Don't flip aria-hidden on the whole app simultaneously if focus hasn't moved yet. Try setting inert or aria-hidden after the dialog receives focus.
Ibrahim Saleh: Also, the announcer text is prepopulated with "Shortcuts" on mount, then we set innerHTML again which triggers a duplicate announcement. Could debounce or only set once.
Keiko Tanaka: Small code example to open safely:
```js
function openShortcuts(){
  const dialog = document.getElementById('shortcuts-dialog');
  dialog.removeAttribute('hidden');
  dialog.setAttribute('role','dialog');
  dialog.setAttribute('aria-modal','true');
  const oldFocus = document.activeElement;
  requestAnimationFrame(()=>{
    dialog.querySelector('h2').focus();
    document.getElementById('app-root').setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');
  });
  dialog.dataset.returnFocus = oldFocus?.id || '';
}
```
Note: use requestAnimationFrame to ensure focus change happens before hiding.
Sasha Lee: Good. Also the keyboard shortcut overlay lists 30 items; VoiceOver users prefer a short summary first: "Showing global shortcuts, 30 items" in an aria-live polite element inside the dialog once it opens. That avoids the long list dump.
Maya Patel: UX copy nit: group the shortcuts by category and add headings with role="heading" and tabindex='-1' so SR users can jump by heading. Also add a "Close" button with aria-label="Close shortcuts" as first focusable element.
Ibrahim Saleh: Another observed issue: pressing Esc closes the overlay but focus moves to the body instead of the trigger key. We should restore focus to the element that opened it (or if keyboard '?' was used, focus back to last focused element). Use the dataset.returnFocus from Keiko's snippet.
Keiko Tanaka: For the visual focus ring, we're using a 1px dotted outline for the dialog close button which disappears on high-contrast. Make it 3px solid using our focus token --focus-ring and test contrast in both themes.
Sasha Lee: a11y-bot: quick scan suggestions: role=dialog missing on #shortcuts-dialog \u274c; duplicate live announcements likely due to double-set innerHTML \u26a0\ufe0f; close-button focus-outline contrast 2.2:1 \u26a0\ufe0f. Auto-report: https://redwood-internal/a11y/2123456789
a11y-bot: Also suggests adding headings for category groups and limiting initial SR announcement to: "Shortcuts overlay. 3 categories. Press Escape to close."
Maya Patel: Great notes. Plan: 1) Change overlay semantics to dialog + aria-modal; 2) Focus first h2 on open, set aria-hidden on app after focus; 3) Debounce live announcer text and only announce short summary; 4) Restore focus on close; 5) Update focus token to --focus-ring and include screenshots for light/dark/HC.
Ibrahim Saleh: I'll open a PR with the JS fix, a small Playwright keyboard E2E sim that opens via '?', tabs through first 3 items, hits Escape and asserts focus returned. Will attach VoiceOver manual steps too.
Keiko Tanaka: I'll adjust the CSS for the close button and add headings for categories.
Sasha Lee: When you add the PR include a short recording of VoiceOver behavior before/after if possible. Tag @eng-runtime for any global inert polyfill needs.
Maya Patel: Thanks team 44d. Small but high-impact. Looking forward to the PR.
